# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What are the two gates that create the Bell state here?\n"
msgstr "Warum hätte ein perfekter Simulator nicht immer genau gleich viele 00-Counts wie 11-Counts?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
"An H gate on qubit 0, followed by a CX gate with qubit 0 as control and qubit 1 as target.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Antwort\">\n"
"Obwohl ein Simulator „perfekt\" ist und zu einem perfekten Bell-Zustand führt, simuliert er dennoch einen inhärent zufälligen Prozess, sodass statistische Schwankungen weiterhin auftreten. Es ist wie 1000 Mal eine Münze zu werfen: Selbst wenn die Chance genau 50-50 steht, bedeutet das nicht, dass du immer genau 500 Mal Kopf und 500 Mal Zahl bekommst.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: Warum könnte ein
# echter Quantencomputer einige 01- oder 10-E
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On an ideal simulator, which two bitstrings should dominate the histogram?\n"
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
"00 and 11 should dominate.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Why wouldn't a perfect simulator always have the exact same number of 00 counts as 11 counts?\n"
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
"Even though a simulator is \"perfect\" and leads to a perfect Bell state, it is still simulating an inherently random process, so statistical fluctuations will still occur. It's like flipping a coin 1000 times: even if there is an exact 50-50 chance of the coin landing on heads or tails, that doesn't mean you'll always get exactly 500 instances of heads and 500 of tails.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Antwort\">\n"
"Weil echte Geräte Rauschen haben. Gates und Messungen sind nicht perfekt, und das kann gelegentliche Fehler einführen.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: Was ist ein
# praktischer Unterschied zwischen Simulatoren und
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Why might a real quantum computer show some 01 or 10 results even though the simulator didn't?\n"
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
"Because real devices have noise. Gates and measurements are not perfect, and that can introduce occasional errors.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What is one practical difference between simulators and real quantum computers besides noise?\n"
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
"Quantum computers can involve queue time, limited availability, and device-specific constraints that affect how circuits run.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Antwort\">\n"
"Quantencomputer können Wartezeiten in der Warteschlange, begrenzte Verfügbarkeit und gerätespezifische Einschränkungen mit sich bringen, die beeinflussen, wie Circuits ausgeführt werden.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

